course: dictionary
lesson: 2716
title: Dimly: a little light, a faint memory
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dimly is a describing word for how something happens. It means with only a little light, so a dimly lit room is not pitch dark, but it is not bright either. «A glow stick in the freezer glows more dimly but lasts longer, because cold slows the reaction down.» Here more dimly means the light is weaker.
explain: Dimly can also mean not clearly. When you dimly remember something, it is faint in your mind, like a song from when you were little. Look at the words around it: if something is hard to see or hard to recall, dimly probably means faintly.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Try "faintly" or "weakly" in place of dimly. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Clue words like lit, glow, shine, remember and aware will often point the way.
fact: Dimly is an adverb: it tells you how something happens, such as how a light shines.
fact: Dimly means with only a little light, not brightly.
fact: Dimly also means not clearly, in a faint or uncertain way.
fact: Useful phrases are dimly lit, dimly remember, dimly aware and shine dimly.
fact: «More dimly» compares two things: the glow stick glows more dimly in the freezer than in the sun.
exercise: «The cave was dimly lit by a single torch.» What does dimly mean here? | *With only a little light | Brightly, with every light on | Full of water | Very loudly
exercise: «A glow stick in the freezer glows more dimly but lasts longer, because cold slows the reaction down.» What does more dimly mean? | Very quickly | With more light, shining brightly | *With less light, shining more weakly | Without any colour at all
exercise: Sam says, «I dimly remember my first day at school.» What does dimly mean here? | Very clearly, every detail | *Not clearly, in a faint way | Angrily | Loudly and happily
test: The bulb shines dimly because the battery is weak. What does dimly mean? | Warmly | Quickly | Brightly | *With only a little light
test: Which phrase means you remember something in a faint, uncertain way? | shine dimly | *dimly remember | dimly aware | brightly lit
exam: Which sentence uses dimly to mean not clearly? | *Ella dimly recalled the name of her first teacher. | The window was wide and open. | The sun shone brightly all day. | The glow stick glowed dimly in the freezer.
